 The HarnessOS x64 Debian artifact is `dist/orca-linux-x64.deb`. Its resources
-include `orca-fork-build.json` naming the full workbench HEAD. Before publication,
-the confined builder must qualify those exact bytes for tailnet-only binding;
-ordinary development builds and loopback-only probes do not qualify an artifact.
+include `orca-fork-build.json` naming the full workbench HEAD and verified series
+and build digests. The Debian data archive uses gzip (`deb.compression: 'gz'`),
+not electron-builder's default xz, so the publisher can inspect it in-process.
+Before publication, the confined builder must qualify those exact bytes for
+tailnet-only binding; development builds and loopback probes do not qualify it.
 
